# Test: the suite's native le binary preserves every checks command's data,
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
# rendering, exit, stream, scope, ordering, negative-case, and filesystem contracts.
# Selftests publish nonempty, uniquely named passing cases; count agrees with JSON
# without fixing the number of cases a gate may add. Source-reading checks still
# inspect the real checkout. The compiles action builds an owned committed module
# in every production matrix flavor, at the unchanged default package floor,
# instead of rebuilding the shared checkout's HEAD inside a UI rendering test.
# Independent real-corpus and tracked-build verification gates remain unchanged.

option=timeout:value=1800s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/le-checks-answers
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
